@AC 1317. Nothing with man is regarded by the Lord except the end.

@1702[2]. Man can look upwards... and can look downwards. Explained.

@1807. "Look towards heaven" (Genesis 15:5). Explained.

@2417. Not to look to doctrinal things. Signified, Explained. @2454, Explained.

@2568[2]. To regard the doctrine of faith from rational things; and... to regard rational things from the doctrine of faith. Explained.

@2584[3]. The doctrine of faith when regarded from truths Divine; and when regarded from what is rational. Explained... To look from the Word is to look from the Lord; whereas to look from reason and knowledge is to look from man.

@3159. "I will look to the right or to the left" (Genesis 24:49) Explained.

@3182. No longer looks at good from truth...

@3324[5]. Doctrinal things regard charity as the end.

@--[6]. In Heaven all are regarded from charity and the derivative faith.

@3913[3]. The natural man looks to self and the world...

