@--[end]. The name "Mizpah" is so called from to "look."

@4221[end]. Regard themselves alone in everything.

@4255[3]. Then Knowledges are regarded from this good; and not good from them.

@4882[3]. If one were to look towards the east, and the other towards the west, to both the good would appear on the right, and the evil on the left.

@5368[end]. When he regards corporeal and worldly things as means...

@5433[2]. If the internal man looks downwards... he cannot possibly look upwards...

@5660[3]. They no longer regard themselves in everything... but they regard the neighbour, etc.

@5949. Scientifics... must regard good as the end.

@6247[2]. He then regards good from truth... He then regards truth from good.

@6402. These look downwards or outwards, because they are not yet in good. But those who are in good... look upwards or inwards.

@6468[3]. Those in Heaven look upwards to the Lord; those in Hell look downwards from Him.

@6952[6]. "The tail" = what is lowest, which looks downwards...

