@AE 112[2]. The interiors of man... actually look whither his love does.

@1174[3]. If he looks to the Lord he is brought out of those Societies...

@Char 1. That the first of charity is to look to the Lord... @2.

@158. That every man who looks to the Lord...

@CanonsNC 28. Redemption. 5. 3. Those who in the world have looked and turned themselves to Heaven or to Hell, look and turn themselves in the same way after death.

Look back.; Respicere.

@AC 2417. "Look not back behind thee" (Genesis 19:17) = that he should not look to doctrinal things. Explained.

@2454. "His wife looked back behind him" (verse 26) that truth averted itself from good, and looked to doctrinal things. Explained.

@6804[10]. To "have respect to them" (Leviticus 26:9) = what is of mercy.

@7122. "Let them not have respect to words of a lie" (Exodus 5:9) = lest they turn themselves to truths.

@7341. "Pharaoh looked back and came to his house" (Exodus 7:23) = thought and reflection from falsities. To "look back" = thought and reflection; for in the spiritual sense to "look back" is not to look with the eyes towards anything, but it is to look with the mind, thus to think and reflect.

@7650. "He looked back and went out from with Pharaoh" (Exodus 10:6) = the privation of apperception and separation... To "look back" = the privation of apperception; for a man is deprived of apperception when truth from the Divine looks back or averts itself; that is, when the man averts himself from it.

@8442. "They looked back to the wilderness" (Exodus 16:10) = recollection of the state of temptation in which they were. To "look back" to anything = thought and reflection, thus also recollection.

@10450. "Moses looked back and descended from the mountain" (Exodus 32:15) = the Word let down from Heaven.

@AE 304[37]. Occurs. @374[13]. @391[23].

Look back.; Retrospicere.

@AC 8505[3]. When a man is acting from affection he is no longer allowed to look back, and to do what is good from truth... If he then looks back... he acts from what is his own. Explained.

Look down.; Despicere.

@HH 208. No Angel of a higher Heaven may look down...

@AR 565. a. See <Look at>.

@CL 477[3]. A certain Angel looking down, heard these things...

@533. The Angels petitioned the Lord to be allowed to look down into the world; and they looked down...

@TCR 77[5]. (The Angels said) We have looked down into the earth at those celebrated for erudition...

@412. The Lord, and, from Him, the Angels, when they look down into the earth...

@SE 5761. On Spirits who looked down. @5786[2]. @5830. @5831. @5839. @5875. @5889. @5929. @5967. @6081.

@AE 187. When the Angels who are in the Heavens look down to those who are in such lumen...

@Coro 14[end]. When the Angels... look down into the earth, they see not one whit of it, but only the Church with men.

Look out.; Prospicere.
Lookout.; Prospectus.

@AC 2219. "They looked out to the faces of Sodom" (Genesis 18:16) = the state of the human race.

@2245. "The men looked out thence" (verse 22) = the Lord's thought from the Divine... To "look out" = to think, Explained. @2684.

@3391. "Abimelech... looked out through a window" (Genesis 26:8) = the doctrine of faith looking to rational things...

@5286. The looking forward -prospectio- of the Natural. Signified, Explained. @5289.

@6760. "He looked out hither and thither, and saw that there was no man" (Exodus 2:12) = prudence as to whether he was in safety.

@6938. Under <Honour>, see this reference.

@8212. "Jehovah looked out to the camp of the Egyptians" (Exodus 14:24) = the extension thence of the Divine influx... Explained.

@8478[2]. It is not contrary to order to look out for one's self and others.

@AE 650[30]. "Its lookout was to the end of the earth" (Daniel 4:11) = its extension even to the ultimates of the Church.

Looker-out. See <Watchman>.

Lookup.; Suspicere. @CL 132[5].

Loop.; Loramentum.

@AC 9605. "Loops" = conjunction. Explained. @9608. @9610. @9623.

